"explanation": "Document 1 states that No. 100 Squadron RAAF (Royal Australian Air Force) was formed at RAAF Station Richmond, New South Wales, on 15 February 1942. New South Wales is a state in Australia. Document 3 corroborates this, stating that in February 1942, No. 100 Squadron, Royal Australian Air Force was formed at RAAF Richmond, near Sydney, from a nucleus of 100 Squadron RAF personnel, and explicitly notes that despite the link to the RAF, the squadron was an RAAF squadron throughout its existence. While Document 3 mentions a separate 'No. 100 Squadron RAF proper' being re-formed in the UK later in 1942, the primary formation of the squadron discussed in the context of the RAAF (which is the main subject of Document 1 and the initial formation described in Document 3) occurred in Australia."
}

